LOCUS       MOZMTZ                     1 bp    DNA     linear   VRT 18-JAN-1996
DEFINITION  Morone saxatilis mitochondrial transfer RNA-Thr, -Pro and -Phe
            genes, control region, and 12S ribosomal RNA (12S rRNA) gene.
ACCESSION   L60529 REGION: 1
VERSION     L60529.1
KEYWORDS    12S ribosomal RNA; control region; ribosomal RNA; transfer RNA;
            transfer RNA-Phe; transfer RNA-Pro; transfer RNA-Thr.
SOURCE      mitochondrion Morone saxatilis (striped sea-bass)
  ORGANISM  Morone saxatilis
            Eukaryota; Metazoa; Chordata; Craniata; Vertebrata; Euteleostomi;
            Actinopterygii; Neopterygii; Teleostei; Neoteleostei;
            Acanthomorphata; Eupercaria; Moronidae; Morone.
REFERENCE   1  (bases 1 to 1)
  AUTHORS   Stabile,J.E. and Wirgin,I.I.
  TITLE     Characterization of heteroplasmy and length variation of the
            striped bass mitochondrial genome
  JOURNAL   Unpublished
COMMENT     Original source text: Mitochondrion Morone saxatilis
            (individual_isolate East Hamptom Specimen 21) adult liver DNA.
            The control region of the M. saxatilis can contain several copies
            of a 121 bp tandem repeat. Length variation among different mtDNA
            haplotypes is due to varying numbers of the tandem repeats.  The
            smallest haplotype contains three copies while the largest can have
            six or more.   The first tandem repeat among all genotypes examined
            to date is truncated relative to the others.
FEATURES             Location/Qualifiers
     source          1
                     /organism="Morone saxatilis"
                     /organelle="mitochondrion"
                     /mol_type="genomic DNA"
                     /isolate="East Hamptom Specimen 21"
                     /db_xref="taxon:34816"
                     /haplotype="C"
                     /tissue_type="liver"
                     /dev_stage="adult"
                     /note="striped bass"
ORIGIN      
        1 c
//

